<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kruševo</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Krushevo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kruševo is a mountain town in the south-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-macedonia">North Macedonia</a>, at about 1,350 metres one of the highest towns in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a>. A prosperous trading centre of Slav, Aromanian and Greek-oriented <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> families under Ottoman rule, it was seized by insurgents in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilinden-preobrazhenie-uprising">Ilinden Uprising</a> of 1903, who proclaimed the short-lived Kruševo Republic. The Ilinden memorial, the Makedonium, stands above the town.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/krusevo.jpg" alt="Kruševo" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Milo van Kovacevic · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kru%C5%A1evo_northern_view.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
